\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{A fine staggered shift includes a sign}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{Golterman and Smit's fine shift translates the
link field and multiplies the shifted fermion
field by a site-dependent sign. Their symmetry
and measure discussion uses periodic or
antiperiodic boundary conditions and an even
number of sites
\citet{pp. 62–63, (2.3)–(2.4), and the paragraph after (2.13)}{goltermansmit1984flavor}.}

\p{In their momentum-block notation the shift
is #{\ue^{\ui p_\mu}\Xi_\mu}, equation (2.31),
and the two Clifford matrix families in (2.27)
commute with one another
\citet{p. 65, (2.26)–(2.31)}{goltermansmit1984flavor}.
The [cochain translation](fdip-00W0) instead
keeps the exterior labels fixed and directly
reindexes the based coefficients. Its generated
algebra in \ref{fdip-00W3} uses that declared
action. Inserting the fine staggered shift
would require an intertwining map between the
two field spaces.}
